he runbook confirms it is left in reporting and operator notes only.\n\n## Cleanup Plan\n\n| flag | action | blockers | rationale |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW` | `keep` | none | Primary live flag controlling preview routing. Actively used in production |\n| `ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2` | `deprecate` | legacy deploy manifests | Legacy alias for ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW. Deprecate once legacy manifests are migrated to use the canonical flag name. |\n| `PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY` | `docs_cleanup` | operator notes reference, telemetry consumers | Remove from runtime code after updating operator notes and confirming no telemetry consumers depend on force_legacy_seen flag. |\n\n## Assumption Ledger\n\n| status | topic | note |\n|---|---|---|\n| observed | ENABLE_SHADOW_PREVIEW runtime branch | Confirmed in runtime.py and test |\n| observed | ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 alias behavior | Confirmed in config.py and runbook |\n| observed | PREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY dead flag | Confirmed in runtime.py and runbook |\n| missing | external telemetry consumers | Cannot verify if external systems depend on force_legacy_seen |\n\nPREVIEW_FORCE_LEGACY is a dead flag that no longer affects runtime branching but remains in the parser for telemetry. Operators may mistakenly believe it affects routing. ENABLE_PREVIEW_V2 is a legacy alias that should be documented as such.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
